        <section style="padding: 4rem 0; background: var(--bg-surface);">
            <div class="container" style="max-width: 800px;">
                <div class="section-header text-center fade-in" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
                    <h2>Common Questions</h2>
                </div>
                <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.5rem;">
                    <div class="glass-panel fade-in" style="padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 12px;">
                        <h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">What is a CAS statement and why does it matter?</h3>
                        <p style="color: var(--text-body); line-height: 1.7; margin: 0;">A <strong>Consolidated Account Statement (CAS)</strong> is an official financial document issued by SEBI-registered Registrar and Transfer Agents (RTAs) such as CAMS and KFintech. It consolidates all your mutual fund transactions across brokers into a single PDF, providing a verifiable, tamper-resistant record of your investments. Arthavi parses this document locally to extract transactions — it never stores or reuses the file.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="glass-panel fade-in" style="padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 12px;">
                        <h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">How does Arthavi calculate XIRR?</h3>
                        <p style="color: var(--text-body); line-height: 1.7; margin: 0;">Arthavi calculates <strong>XIRR (Extended Internal Rate of Return)</strong> using your actual cash flows — every SIP installment, lumpsum investment, redemption, and dividend payout — with precise transaction dates extracted from your CAS or manual entries. This produces a time-weighted return figure that accounts for the timing of each investment, which is the industry-standard metric for measuring portfolio performance in India.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="glass-panel fade-in" style="padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 12px;">
                        <h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Why is Arthavi more private than other portfolio trackers?</h3>
                        <p style="color: var(--text-body); line-height: 1.7; margin: 0;">Most portfolio apps in India require demat account linking, which grants them read/write access to your broker and exposes your holdings to their data infrastructure. Arthavi requires neither. You upload only a CAS document — a read-only, SEBI-regulated file — to your own device. Arthavi does not sell, share, or monetize your data to third parties, brokers, or advertisers. Phone numbers are not even mandatory for signup.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="glass-panel fade-in" style="padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 12px;">
                        <h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Can Arthavi help detect portfolio overlap?</h3>
                        <p style="color: var(--text-body); line-height: 1.7; margin: 0;">Yes. Arthavi's <strong>Ask AI</strong> feature analyzes your holdings across mutual funds and stocks to detect sector and stock-level overlap. For example, if Mirae Large Cap and Axis Bluechip both hold HDFC Bank and Reliance as top holdings, Arthavi flags this as a potential concentration risk — helping you avoid redundancy and improve diversification.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
